<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSteamLock_BiomeWiring.xml     UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S1. Wires the permanent steam lock
  (Defs/GameConditionDefs/RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml) onto RUT_TheScald as a
  PATCH rather than a direct edit to RUT_TheScald.xml's own
  biomeMapConditions field — RUT_ScaldSteamLock only exists when
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active (MayRequire-gated def), so a
  bare <li> baked directly into the BiomeDef would be a dangling
  cross-reference the moment that mod is absent. Gate: PatchOperationFindMod
  on the kit's display name, wrapping the whole Conditional below. ⚠️
  MayRequire on an <Operation> is INERT (MEASURED 2026-09-17 against 1.6
  source — ModContentPack.LoadPatches never reads the attribute); the
  Conditional's own xpath test (does RUT_TheScald already carry
  biomeMapConditions) is structural, not gated on the absent mod, so
  without a real gate this patch would run every load and inject the
  dangling reference regardless. FindMod is the only real per-operation
  gate.

  RUT_TheScald.xml carries no <biomeMapConditions> node at all today (only
  wildAnimals/baseWeatherCommonalities/terrainsByFertility), so this adds
  the whole element rather than appending an <li> to an existing one.

  SCALD_STEAM_WEATHER_DESIGN_1 step 4, 2026-09-26: a SECOND permanent
  condition rides the same patch — RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier, the grant half of
  the steam exposure clock. It is a separate GameConditionDef rather than a
  field on the lock because the lock's class (RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse)
  has no carrierHediff and the class that does has no periodic lapse; see
  RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier.xml's own header for why neither was extended. The
  two cannot fight: the carrier sets no forcedWeather.

  TERMINALBIOMES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 step 2, 2026-09-25: moved into this mod from
  UtinniPatches (frozen twin, same folder there). xpath retargeted
  RUT_TheScald -> RM_TheScald per the item's own §7(a) instruction — this
  file physically relocated with the rest of the S1 kit.
  -->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Environmental Hazards Kit</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheScald"]/biomeMapConditions</xpath>
      <!-- Element absent (the shipped state): add it with BOTH permanent
           conditions at once. -->
      <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheScald"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <biomeMapConditions>
            <li>RUT_ScaldSteamLock</li>
            <li>RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier</li>
          </biomeMapConditions>
        </value>
      </nomatch>
      <!-- Element already present (some other mod or a future direct edit
           put it there): append only the carrier, which is the entry this
           2026-09-26 pass adds. Appending the lock too would risk a
           duplicate; the nomatch branch above is the one that ships. -->
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheScald"]/biomeMapConditions</xpath>
        <value>
          <li>RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier</li>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
